  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> be a relation on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8477;</mi></math>, given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>{</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>:</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt></math> is an irrational number <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>}</mo></math>. Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Reflexive but neither symmetric nor transitive",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "Reflexive and transitive but not symmetric",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Reflexive and symmetric but not transitive",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "An equivalence relation",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>:</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>is</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>irrational</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><strong>Reflexive:</strong></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt></math>&nbsp;is irrational.</p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi></math>, hence&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;is reflexive.</p><p>Given:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>:</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>is</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>irrational</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><strong>Symmetric:</strong></p><p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi></math>, then</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt></math>&nbsp;is irrational.</p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt></math>&nbsp;is not necessarily irrational, since if&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>Z</mi></math>, then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt></math>&nbsp;is irrational., but&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt></math>&nbsp;is not irrational.</p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi><menclose notation=\"updiagonalstrike\"><mo>&#8658;</mo></menclose><mfenced><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi></math>, hence&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;not symmetric</p><p><strong>Transitive:</strong></p><p>Take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>So, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> but <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8713;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> which means relation is not transitive.</p>"
  }
}